35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"It turns out one neighbor is doing almost all the complaining! Also, nobody wants to be the ""bad guy"" and tell others their bags are late. We really need a friendly solution!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My visit to the bin house was a bit surprising. It seems that in the heat of August, the smell can actually become worse because it's so hard to clean inside. We must be careful.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The frontages are inconsistent; some are too narrow for a bay, and one is blocked by a driveway. Also, the paperwork for a permanent build is tedious, requiring a site plan and four months of waiting.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,The bin house smelled super sour! It's like a giant stinky box in the summer. And those supervised mornings take almost an hour! That's way too long to just stand there.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is enlightening to hear your findings. I have discovered that a permanent shelter is quite a costly venture, and our current open system is quietly draining our funds through constant maintenance and fees.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, if the paperwork is that long and some spots are too narrow, maybe a permanent build isn't the best way to keep everyone happy? We don't want more stress!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, it sounds like you had quite an experience with that smell! I agree with Kenji; we should find a way that doesn't put too much pressure on anyone or our patience.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, I agree. A permanent structure is impractical given the physical constraints of the frontages and the bureaucratic burden. We should avoid any solution that requires excessive paperwork or rigid placement.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, if the open system is draining money, maybe we need a change! But @Shizue, I really don't want a stinky box. And standing around for an hour sounds super boring!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,Life teaches us that the most sustainable paths are those that balance our physical comfort with our financial peace. We must find a solution that is neither a burden on our time nor a strain on our wallets.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"If we can't agree on who should police the bags, maybe we should avoid any system that makes one person the ""boss"" of the bins. That would just cause more fighting!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Kenji. It would be so sad if our efforts to fix the bins ended up hurting our friendships. We should choose something that lets us remain kind to one another.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. Beyond the social friction, we must consider the actual labor involved. If a system requires constant supervision or frequent administrative updates, it will inevitably fall on one person's shoulders, which is unsustainable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that's exactly it! It's not fair if one person does all the work or has the stinky bins at their gate forever. We have to make sure everyone takes a turn!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"True fairness is not merely about dividing the work, but about ensuring that no one is burdened beyond their means. Let us remember that our neighbors' circumstances vary, and a gentle approach is always best.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm really glad we're all thinking about fairness! Let's make sure we pick something that doesn't make anyone feel targeted, so we can all keep being great neighbors.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
51,2,4,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I feel so warmed by how much you all care for one another. Let's keep this gentle spirit as we look at our options.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
53,2,4,pass,Shizue,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I agree. We must prioritize a system that is low-maintenance and doesn't create a hidden workload for a single volunteer. Let's be very careful about the time commitment required for the options we are presented with.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
